// The storage challenge policy on azdatalake's dfs pipeline, case by
// case as the Go program runs it (challengevectors_test.xo): a
// recording fake credential and a fake service that answers each
// path's scripted 401s, then 201. No Entra calls.

use std/http
use github.com/xo-lang/azure/azcore
use github.com/xo-lang/azure/policy

const CEP: Str = "http://chal.dfs.example.test"

const CH: Str = "Bearer authorization_uri=\"https://login.example.test/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/oauth2/authorize\" resource_id=\"https://a.example.test\""

/// A fake credential that writes each token request to `log`.
struct RecCred {
  log: Mutex[List[Str]]
  n: Atomic[Int]
}

fn (c: RecCred) get_token(opts: azcore.TokenRequestOptions) -> azcore.AccessToken ! azcore.AuthErr uses (net.dial, clock, rand) {
  let n = c.n.add(1)
  c.log.with(fn(var xs: List[Str]) { xs.push("  token ${n}: scopes=${opts.scopes.join(",")} tenant=${go_quote(opts.tenant_id)} claims=${go_quote(opts.claims)} cae=${opts.enable_cae}") })
  Ok(azcore.AccessToken{token: Secret.new("tok-${n}"), expires_on: Time.from_unix_millis(4102444800000)})
}

test "the dfs pipeline answers storage challenges as Go's" {
  let log = Mutex[List[Str]].new([])
  let script = Mutex[Map[Str, List[Str]]].new({})
  os.net.handle("PUT ${CEP}/fs1/{d}", fn(req: http.Request) -> http.Response {
    log.with(fn(var xs: List[Str]) { xs.push("  send PUT ${req.path} auth=${go_quote(req.header("Authorization") ?? "")}") })
    let next = script.with(fn(var m: Map[Str, List[Str]]) -> Str? {
      let rs = m.get(req.path) ?? []
      if rs.is_empty() {
        return None
      }
      m[req.path] = rs[1..rs.len()]
      Some(rs[0])
    })
    match next {
      Some(a) => {
        let r = http.text(401, "").with_header("Date", "Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:52:15 GMT")
        if a == "" { r } else { r.add_header("WWW-Authenticate", a) }
      }
      None => http.text(201, "").with_header("Date", "Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:52:15 GMT")
    }
  })
  var out: List[Str] = []
  for (name, audience, replies) in [("plain", "", []), ("audience", "https://acct1.example.test/", []), ("challenge", "", [CH]), ("nochallenge", "", [""])] {
    script.with(fn(var m: Map[Str, List[Str]]) { m["/fs1/d-${name}"] = replies })
    let opts = ClientOptions{client: policy.ClientOptions{retry: policy.RetryOptions{max_retries: -1}}, audience: audience, insecure_allow_credential_with_http: true}
    log.reset(["directory.Client ${name}:"])
    let dc = new_directory_client(os.net, os.clock, os.rand, "${CEP}/fs1/d-${name}", RecCred{log: log, n: Atomic.new(0)}, opts)
    for _ in 0..2 {
      let l = match dc.create() {
        Ok(_) => "  ok"
        Err(Response(e)) => "  status ${e.status_code}"
        Err(e) => "  err: ${e.display()}"
      }
      log.with(fn(var xs: List[Str]) { xs.push(l) })
    }
    out = out + log.with_read(fn(xs: List[Str]) -> List[Str] { xs })
  }
  expect(out) == CHALLENGE_OUTPUT
}
